<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani stock exchange's capitalisation rises.</title>
<headline>Pakistani stock exchange's capitalisation rises.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Karachi Stock Exchange said on Friday its listed firms' market capitalisation rose to 527.167 billion rupees in February from 500.613 billion in January.</p>
<p>Details are listed below:</p>
<p>						     February   January</p>
<p> Listed capital (billion rupees)	   203.347    202.939</p>
<p> Market capitalisation (billion rupees)  527.167    500.613</p>
<p> Turnover of shares (n million rupees)   874.628    605.041</p>
<p> KSE 100 index  (points)		   1,667.05   1,534.21</p>
<p> KSE all share index (points)	    1,071.74   1,017.76</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
